The problem asks for the total distance James runs in a week. To calculate this, we first determine the total number of sprints he completes in a week. James runs **3 sprints per session** and does this **3 times a week**. Thus, the total number of sprints is:

$$
3 \text{ sprints/session} \times 3 \text{ sessions/week} = 9 \text{ sprints/week}
$$

Each sprint is **60 meters**, so multiplying the total number of sprints by the length of one sprint gives the total distance:

$$
9 \text{ sprints} \times 60 \text{ meters/sprint} = 540 \text{ meters}
$$

