A raspberry bush has 6 clusters of 20 fruit each and 67 individual fruit scattered across the bush. 

1. Calculate the number of raspberries in the clusters:
   $$
   6 \text{ clusters} \times 20 \text{ fruit per cluster} = 120 \text{ raspberries}
   $$

2. Add the individual raspberries:
   $$
   120 \text{ raspberries} + 67 \text{ individual raspberries} = 187 \text{ raspberries}
   $$

Thus, the total number of raspberries is $\boxed{187}$.

